  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Africa-Europe Digital Innovation Bridge 2.0 (AEDIB 2.0)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;b&gt;The AEDIB 2.0 project&lt;/b&gt; (Africa-Europe Digital Innovation Bridge 2.0) is part of the regional Team Europe Initiative (TEI) D4D for the Digital Economy and Society in Sub-Saharan Africa, contributing specifically to the entrepreneurship and skills pillar.  The overall objective of the project is to strengthen&amp;nbsp;digital transformation and the green transition by fostering stronger partnerships for digital entrepreneurship and innovation between Africa and Europe.  The specific objectives (outcomes) of the project are:&amp;nbsp;(1) Enhance policies that promote digital entrepreneurship and innovation, (2) Strengthen digital innovation ecosystems for digital transformation and green transition and, (3) Improve access to finance for innovative ventures, including women-led enterprises, that contribute to digital transformation and the green transition.</narrative>
  </description>
